+    Reweight the single-scattering estimate to approximate higher-order scattering. The total volumetric contribution $L$ is a sum of $N$ octaves:
+    $$ L = \sum_{i=0}^{N-1} L_i $$
+    where each octave $L_i$ is defined as:
+    $$ L_i = \sigma_s(p, \omega_i) (\gamma \cdot \text{Albedo}(p, \omega_i))^i L_{light}(\omega_i) P'_i(\omega_i, \omega_o) T_i $$
+    *   $L_{light}(\omega_i)$: Incident radiance from the light source.
