 ## Background
-*   **Origin:** Proposed by Hu, Zhu, Lin, and Zhang (Nanjing University/Shandong University) in 2026 [S1].
-*   **Development:** Builds on the insight that dense hair behaves like an anisotropic participating medium at the scale of multiple scattering. It adapts the single-to-multiple scattering approximation from Wrenninge et al. [2013] to handle spectral and angular characteristics of hair, using the Yan et al. [2017a] double-cylinder fur model for single-fiber reflectance [S1].
-*   **Usage:** Implemented in Mitsuba 0.6 [S1].
+The method was proposed by Hu, Zhu, Lin, and Zhang, building on the observation that dense hair aggregates behave like an anisotropic participating medium [S1]. It addresses the limitations of prior approximations like Dual Scattering and Fur BSSRDF, which often yield dry or blurred appearances in dense hair [S1]. The implementation was demonstrated in Mitsuba 0.6 [S1]. Parameters were obtained via numerical optimization using Ceres Solver with an L1 loss on a scene with three area lights [S1].
 
